 {'family':'unix_entropy_descriptor_retry_and_log_frontier','finding':'Pinned unixRandomness zeroes the buffer and obtains pid. Outside SQLITE_TEST/OMIT_RANDOMNESS it calls robust_open(/dev/urandom,O_RDONLY,0), then osRead retrying EINTR or falls back to time+pid on open failure, then robust_close. robust_open can repeat osOpen on EINTR, repair too-small descriptor allocation by closing, sqlite3_log warning and opening /dev/null O_RDONLY, and set close-on-exec. For this exact O_RDONLY/m0 call, its explicit O_EXCL|O_CREAT unlink and m!=0 chmod branches do not apply; this is not a general namespace/metadata/VFS side-effect proof. robust_close does not retry close failure; it calls the error logger and may leave a descriptor. sqlite3_log emits through configured xLog only; its renderer invokes that callback, not an unconditional stderr or journald write. osOpen/osRead/osClose/log providers and syscall-table overrides remain source/runtime obligations. Do not infer one open/read, finite retry count, no log production, no leaked descriptor, actual Linux execution or cleanup authority.'},
